3. Prior treatment with a gene product;
4. Plasmapheresis with symptoms of compression (e.g., pleural effusion, abdominal effusion);
5. Patients with cardiac involvement and gastrointestinal involvement;
6. Autoimmune disease requiring systemic immunosuppressive therapy (e.g., Crohn's disease, rheumatoid arthritis, systemic lupus) within 2 years prior to the start of screening;
